{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"the-girl-who-asked-why","version":1,"title":"The Girl Who Asked Why","ageTiers":["7-8","9-10"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Ayeyi always asked why. Why is the sky blue? Why do birds fly? One day in class she asked, ‘Do heavy things fall faster than light things?’","sentences":["Ayeyi always asked why.","Why is the sky blue?","Why do birds fly?","One day in class she asked, ‘Do heavy things fall faster than light things?’"],"alt":"A girl puts up her hand with a question mark above her head.","image":{"hash":"sha256:af3b7878147016c18e2e4961b69026c603c6cc196d6d628060873480a5c92bd7","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:f3deb6cff27778219cbe78ff27bdeddc74faaef5dca02ec7b6580895de9b675e","durationMs":14320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2640],[2640,4805],[4805,6732],[6732,14320]],"words":[[0,595],[595,1308],[1308,1903],[1903,2640],[2640,2997],[2997,3235],[3235,3592],[3592,3949],[3949,4805],[4805,5162],[5162,5400],[5400,5994],[5994,6732],[6732,7089],[7089,7445],[7445,7683],[7683,8278],[8278,8635],[8635,9420],[9420,9658],[9658,10252],[10252,10966],[10966,11442],[11442,12155],[12155,12631],[12631,13226],[13226,14320]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"Some pupils said yes. Some said no. ‘I think a stone falls faster than a pencil,’ said Ayeyi. ‘Let us not guess,’ said Mr Marfo. ‘Let us test it.’","sentences":["Some pupils said yes.","Some said no.","‘I think a stone falls faster than a pencil,’ said Ayeyi.","‘Let us not guess,’ said Mr Marfo.","‘Let us test it.’"],"alt":"A teacher smiles and holds up a stone and a pencil in front of the class.","image":{"hash":"sha256:52f95a9829e8ba6b4240efa275421f972a1c8d72e0a4fb081095b8a4ce59930a","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:d94744d8633fd86cee063480302c9616594313f998b6bda03e9a0a679b164789","durationMs":15000,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2440],[2440,4034],[4034,9807],[9807,13285],[13285,15000]],"words":[[0,483],[483,1208],[1208,1691],[1691,2440],[2440,2923],[2923,3406],[3406,4034],[4034,4155],[4155,4758],[4758,4879],[4879,5483],[5483,6087],[6087,6812],[6812,7295],[7295,7415],[7415,8333],[8333,8816],[8816,9807],[9807,10169],[10169,10411],[10411,10773],[10773,11570],[11570,12053],[12053,12295],[12295,13285],[13285,13647],[13647,13889],[13889,14372],[14372,15000]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"‘A fair test has rules,’ said Mr Marfo. ‘Drop both things from the same height. Drop them at the same time. Do it three times.’ He took them to the playground, to a soft patch of sand.","sentences":["‘A fair test has rules,’ said Mr Marfo.","‘Drop both things from the same height.","Drop them at the same time.","Do it three times.’ He took them to the playground, to a soft patch of sand."],"alt":"A teacher and a girl stand at the edge of a sand patch with a stone and a pencil.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d6c61c2937b214d561f399d1b1eba88eed197eadb860c315d6253269c2b9ce3f","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:e150e348b943bee081b095f3aa9578230e2e8ed8aff8adc244dbaa76b899895d","durationMs":16360,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3435],[3435,7017],[7017,9552],[9552,16360]],"words":[[0,105],[105,524],[524,943],[943,1257],[1257,1948],[1948,2367],[2367,2577],[2577,3435],[3435,3854],[3854,4273],[4273,4902],[4902,5321],[5321,5635],[5635,6054],[6054,7017],[7017,7436],[7436,7855],[7855,8065],[8065,8379],[8379,8798],[8798,9552],[9552,9762],[9762,9971],[9971,10495],[10495,11354],[11354,11563],[11563,11982],[11982,12401],[12401,12610],[12610,12925],[12925,14140],[14140,14349],[14349,14454],[14454,14873],[14873,15396],[15396,15606],[15606,16360]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Ayeyi held the stone in one hand and the pencil in the other. ‘One, two, three, drop!’ Thud! They landed at almost the same time. ‘They did not fall at different speeds!’ she said.","sentences":["Ayeyi held the stone in one hand and the pencil in the other.","‘One, two, three, drop!’ Thud!","They landed at almost the same time.","‘They did not fall at different speeds!’ she said."],"alt":"A girl drops a stone and a pencil at the same time onto sand.","image":{"hash":"sha256:0c2fb486ed8f3dd641034fcd044a52953a80fe8621acb282ce9d09954c44b7c7","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:45975d162d53cbdc76e3f7b508c41388dc39cdf86ad9df8bebf6902dca3680a1","durationMs":20040,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,6494],[6494,10324],[10324,14409],[14409,20040]],"words":[[0,634],[634,1142],[1142,1522],[1522,2156],[2156,2410],[2410,2790],[2790,3298],[3298,3678],[3678,4059],[4059,4820],[4820,5073],[5073,5454],[5454,6494],[6494,7077],[7077,7661],[7661,8498],[8498,9411],[9411,10324],[10324,10832],[10832,11593],[11593,11846],[11846,12607],[12607,12988],[12988,13495],[13495,14409],[14409,14916],[14916,15296],[15296,15677],[15677,16184],[16184,16438],[16438,17579],[17579,18746],[18746,19127],[19127,20040]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"Next, Mr Marfo gave her two sheets of the same paper. He crumpled one into a ball. ‘Drop the flat one and the ball,’ he said. ‘Guess first.’ ‘The same?’ said Ayeyi.","sentences":["Next, Mr Marfo gave her two sheets of the same paper.","He crumpled one into a ball.","‘Drop the flat one and the ball,’ he said.","‘Guess first.’ ‘The same?’ said Ayeyi."],"alt":"A teacher crumples one sheet of paper while a girl holds a flat sheet.","image":{"hash":"sha256:f7755c75add04c80a6599b8ad1b0280ec65f103c88f20c4a65b858eea9590ad7","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:f4b7b9e9832071d07dfba80006bedd7eee0f040244d9eb95a3030769e3bf2755","durationMs":16880,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5467],[5467,8476],[8476,12630],[12630,16880]],"words":[[0,669],[669,907],[907,1504],[1504,1982],[1982,2340],[2340,2698],[2698,3414],[3414,3653],[3653,4011],[4011,4489],[4489,5467],[5467,5706],[5706,6661],[6661,7019],[7019,7497],[7497,7616],[7616,8476],[8476,8953],[8953,9311],[9311,9789],[9789,10147],[10147,10505],[10505,10863],[10863,11532],[11532,11771],[11771,12630],[12630,13227],[13227,14206],[14206,14564],[14564,15424],[15424,15901],[15901,16880]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"She dropped them. The crumpled ball landed first. The flat sheet floated down slowly. ‘Why?’ she asked. ‘Air pushes up on the flat paper more,’ said Mr Marfo. ‘It is the shape that matters, not only the weight.’","sentences":["She dropped them.","The crumpled ball landed first.","The flat sheet floated down slowly.","‘Why?’ she asked.","‘Air pushes up on the flat paper more,’ said Mr Marfo.","‘It is the shape that matters, not only the weight.’"],"alt":"A crumpled ball of paper lands first while a flat sheet floats down.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d1e99e7c125408abe65564c3fad63c6da394ca873bf7c579aa9823cb6bffae13","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:4720e01a741234eddb87a2775170874ecf12061cd6c2f851b50f1e4a093549b4","durationMs":26240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2445],[2445,6596],[6596,11173],[11173,13646],[13646,20014],[20014,26240]],"words":[[0,426],[426,1421],[1421,2445],[2445,2871],[2871,4008],[4008,4577],[4577,5430],[5430,6596],[6596,7022],[7022,7591],[7591,8301],[8301,9296],[9296,9865],[9865,11173],[11173,12054],[12054,12480],[12480,13646],[13646,14072],[14072,14925],[14925,15210],[15210,15494],[15494,15920],[15920,16489],[16489,17200],[17200,17996],[17996,18564],[18564,18848],[18848,20014],[20014,20298],[20298,20583],[20583,21009],[21009,21720],[21720,22288],[22288,23511],[23511,23937],[23937,24506],[24506,24932],[24932,26240]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"Ayeyi drew a table in her notebook. She wrote what she dropped, what she thought and what happened. ‘A scientist writes down the results,’ said Mr Marfo. ‘Then others can check them.’","sentences":["Ayeyi drew a table in her notebook.","She wrote what she dropped, what she thought and what happened.","‘A scientist writes down the results,’ said Mr Marfo.","‘Then others can check them.’"],"alt":"A girl writes a table of results in her notebook.","image":{"hash":"sha256:e28d2e1f303d4f88f363a0eb0dd66edba92662d7d9c5f25dd708616a1758ee82","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:362b69419d66bd346457c453f7686a40f0a7263a8a3e5d9820658105ed151dec","durationMs":16600,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3278],[3278,9141],[9141,13952],[13952,16600]],"words":[[0,525],[525,946],[946,1051],[1051,1576],[1576,1786],[1786,2101],[2101,3278],[3278,3593],[3593,4118],[4118,4539],[4539,4854],[4854,5757],[5757,6178],[6178,6493],[6493,7228],[7228,7544],[7544,7964],[7964,9141],[9141,9246],[9246,10191],[10191,10822],[10822,11242],[11242,11557],[11557,12461],[12461,12881],[12881,13091],[13091,13952],[13952,14373],[14373,15003],[15003,15318],[15318,15844],[15844,16600]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"‘I thought I knew the answer,’ said Ayeyi. ‘But I did not.’ Mr Marfo smiled. ‘Now you know how to find out,’ he said. ‘That is the best kind of knowing.’ The end.","sentences":["‘I thought I knew the answer,’ said Ayeyi.","‘But I did not.’ Mr Marfo smiled.","‘Now you know how to find out,’ he said.","‘That is the best kind of knowing.’ The end."],"alt":"A girl and her teacher look at a notebook of results in the sunshine.","image":{"hash":"sha256:293bf31479615db0f8c5424b02a43007e26f1585e08ae883f0c98b7f9962aea2","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:32eab5325ea415354e18501b0ccf56d2db1754303d064e57836fd9c1e0830470","durationMs":16120,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4231],[4231,7705],[7705,11582],[11582,16120]],"words":[[0,118],[118,945],[945,1064],[1064,1536],[1536,1891],[1891,2789],[2789,3262],[3262,4231],[4231,4585],[4585,4704],[4704,5058],[5058,5791],[5791,6027],[6027,6618],[6618,7705],[7705,8060],[8060,8415],[8415,8887],[8887,9242],[9242,9478],[9478,9951],[9951,10495],[10495,10731],[10731,11582],[11582,12055],[12055,12291],[12291,12645],[12645,13118],[13118,13591],[13591,13827],[13827,15033],[15033,15387],[15387,16120]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"why-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":4,"question":"What happened when Ayeyi dropped the stone and the pencil?","options":["They landed at almost the same time","The stone flew away","The pencil floated"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"why-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":6,"question":"What did Mr Marfo say makes the flat paper fall slowly?","options":["Air pushes up on it","It is magic","It is heavier"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"why-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":6,"targetSound":"wh","prompt":"Which words start with the wh sound, like why?","options":["why","what","drop","when"],"correctIndexes":[0,1,3]},{"id":"why-p1","type":"prediction","afterPage":5,"prompt":"A flat paper and a crumpled ball are dropped. Which lands first? Tell a friend.","options":["The crumpled ball","The flat paper"]},{"id":"why-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the story in order.","items":["Ayeyi asked her question.","Mr Marfo explained a fair test.","Ayeyi dropped the stone and the pencil.","Ayeyi wrote the results in a table."]},{"id":"why-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Ayeyi learned that testing is better than guessing. How do you feel when you find something out?","feelingOptions":["Curious","Proud","Surprised","Excited"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"test","definition":"A way to find out if something is true.","pages":[2,3]},{"word":"crumpled","definition":"Squeezed into a small, rough ball.","pages":[5,6]},{"word":"results","definition":"What you find out from a test.","pages":[7]}],"assets":{"sha256:af3b7878147016c18e2e4961b69026c603c6cc196d6d628060873480a5c92bd7":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-girl-who-asked-why/page1-1.webp","bytes":64770,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:f3deb6cff27778219cbe78ff27bdeddc74faaef5dca02ec7b6580895de9b675e":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/f3deb6cff277.mp3","bytes":115244,"t